    <string name="gym_lifts_import_summary_pv_header">PV</string>
    <string name="gym_lifts_import_summary_mev_tooltip">Maintenance Volume (MV) — the weekly fractional sets needed to hold muscle. Population default is 4 sets (5–6 for more advanced lifters); your logs may nudge this per muscle.</string>
    <string name="gym_lifts_import_summary_mav_tooltip">Pareto Volume (PV) — growth before obvious diminishing returns. Estimated from your √ dose–response curve; roughly 13 sets/week at the global prior.</string>
    <string name="gym_lifts_import_summary_mrv_tooltip">Recoverability Ceiling (RC) — the highest weekly fractional sets you can plan before recovery becomes the limiter. Not a measured hypertrophy peak; default planning cap is 20 sets.</string>
    <string name="gym_lifts_import_summary_headroom_tooltip">Headroom — whether your logged volume looks like there is room to add sets (room to grow), you are in a steady range, you may already be near your useful weekly max, or we need more data to tell.</string>
